1
00:00:01,900 --> 00:00:22,300
A Real Stewart

2
00:00:22,300 --> 00:00:25,485
There's nothing more joyous than the arrival of a new baby.

3
00:00:25,485 --> 00:00:27,356
I am so excited. Mother!

4
00:00:27,356 --> 00:00:30,400
Just imagine--Marilyn and Richard must be thrilled!

5
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:32,100
Oh, a new baby!

6
00:00:32,100 --> 00:00:36,800
Max ... Max ... Max.

7
00:00:36,800 --> 00:00:42,400
Oh, it's a sweet-sounding name for a sweet little boy.

8
00:00:42,400 --> 00:00:44,700
My first grandchild.

9
00:00:44,700 --> 00:00:47,300
And my first nephew.

10
00:00:47,300 --> 00:00:50,400
Isn't he just adorable?

11
00:00:50,400 --> 00:00:53,100
He looks a lot like you, Mom. He does.

12
00:00:53,100 --> 00:00:56,293
Do you think so?

13
00:00:56,293 --> 00:00:58,900
Well, I guess. He does look a lot like Richard,

14
00:00:58,900 --> 00:01:02,300
and I guess he looks a lot like me.

15
00:01:02,300 --> 00:01:05,800
Oh, he's got Richard's eyes, though.

16
00:01:05,800 --> 00:01:09,300
I really want Harry and Michelle to see Max.

17
00:01:09,300 --> 00:01:10,524
When are they coming?

18
00:01:10,524 --> 00:01:13,900
Tomorrow. Harry has an account to work on today.

19
00:01:13,900 --> 00:01:18,096
Yes, he does have Richard's eyes. Big blue eyes.

20
00:01:18,096 --> 00:01:20,400
[01:20.17]The baby even looks at you like Richard does.

21
00:01:20,400 --> 00:01:22,751
Well, children usually resemble their parents.

22
00:01:22,751 --> 00:01:23,800
It's true.

23
00:01:23,800 --> 00:01:26,700
Michelle is a lot like Harry in so many ways.

24
00:01:26,700 --> 00:01:31,600
And she's shy with new people, just like he is.

25
00:01:31,600 --> 00:01:34,100
You really like Michelle, don't you?

26
00:01:34,100 --> 00:01:36,953
Yes. I'm very fond of her.

27
00:01:36,953 --> 00:01:41,400
And Harry, too?

28
00:01:41,400 --> 00:01:42,188
Well ...

29
00:01:42,188 --> 00:01:44,952
Uh, it's four-thirty. Oh my!

30
00:01:44,952 --> 00:01:47,400
Marilyn and Richard will be home from the hospital any minute,

31
00:01:47,400 --> 00:01:49,300
and we must prepare this room.

32
00:01:49,300 --> 00:01:52,400
Where will we put all the presents?

33
00:01:52,400 --> 00:01:55,212
Well, let's take everything to the living room.

34
00:01:55,212 --> 00:01:58,700
Marilyn and Richard and the baby need the space.

35
00:01:58,700 --> 00:02:01,600
It's crowded in here.

36
00:02:01,600 --> 00:02:03,600
The welcome sign is up:

37
00:02:03,600 --> 00:02:05,500
"Welcome home, Max."

38
00:02:05,500 --> 00:02:07,700
Isn't it exciting, Grandpa?

39
00:02:07,700 --> 00:02:10,000
Your first great-grandchild.

40
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:14,146
Yes. Yes, sir.

41
00:02:14,146 --> 00:02:18,100
A great-grandchild. A great-grandson.

42
00:02:18,100 --> 00:02:21,651
Another generation to carry on the Stewart name.

43
00:02:21,651 --> 00:02:23,180
I love you, Grandpa.

44
00:02:23,180 --> 00:02:27,465
You make me feel so proud to be part of our family.

45
00:02:27,465 --> 00:02:29,300
One day, you'll have your own family,

46
00:02:29,300 --> 00:02:33,000
and I'll be proud to be part of it.

47
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:35,900
Now you understand my feelings, Susan.

48
00:02:35,900 --> 00:02:40,200
I'm Grandpa's daughter-in-law, but I feel like a Stewart.

49
00:02:40,200 --> 00:02:42,826
He's always made me feel like his own daughter.

50
00:02:42,826 --> 00:02:43,600
Well,

51
00:02:43,600 --> 00:02:49,600
that's because you're so much like us--wonderful!

52
00:02:49,600 --> 00:02:55,600
Mom, got it.

53
00:02:55,600 --> 00:02:58,000
This will make a nice gift for Marilyn and Richard.

54
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:00,800
They can keep a record of all of the important dates

55
00:03:00,800 --> 00:03:02,900
and information about Max's life here.

56
00:03:02,900 --> 00:03:04,900
Let's see.

57
00:03:04,900 --> 00:03:07,900
Name: Max Stewart.

58
00:03:07,900 --> 00:03:10,200
Does he have a middle name?

59
00:03:10,200 --> 00:03:14,200
No, just Max. I like that.

60
00:03:14,200 --> 00:03:16,700
No middle name. No middle initial.

61
00:03:16,700 --> 00:03:19,700
Like me. I'm Malcolm Stewart.

62
00:03:19,700 --> 00:03:22,800
Just Malcolm Stewart.

63
00:03:22,800 --> 00:03:24,800
And Max has your initials, Grandpa:

64
00:03:24,800 --> 00:03:31,656
Uh, it must mean something.

65
00:03:31,656 --> 00:03:35,100
Weight: eight pounds six ounces.

66
00:03:35,100 --> 00:03:38,400
Eight-six. Big boy!

67
00:03:38,400 --> 00:03:40,200
All the Stewart men were big.

68
00:03:40,200 --> 00:03:43,100
Well, Robbie was eight pounds two ounces,

69
00:03:43,100 --> 00:03:45,600
and Richard was eight pounds three.

70
00:03:45,600 --> 00:03:48,000
And me?

71
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:50,300
Eight pounds six.

72
00:03:50,300 --> 00:03:53,600
You were big, just like Max.

73
00:03:53,600 --> 00:03:56,000
Eight pounds six, just like me.

74
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:59,000
That's nice. Length. Length?

75
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:02,600
Richard says Max is twenty-one inches long.

76
00:04:02,600 --> 00:04:05,700
Twenty-one inches.

77
00:04:05,700 --> 00:04:08,300
Is that tall or average or what?

78
00:04:08,300 --> 00:04:12,500
Tall. All the Stewart men are tall.

79
00:04:12,500 --> 00:04:18,339
Well, Grandpa, you're about five-nine or five-ten.

80
00:04:18,339 --> 00:04:21,674
I wouldn't call that tall.

81
00:04:21,674 --> 00:04:23,669
I take after my mother's family.

82
00:04:23,669 --> 00:04:29,074
They were ... they were ... they were average.

83
00:04:29,074 --> 00:04:36,300
Mother: Marilyn. Father: Richard.

84
00:04:36,300 --> 00:04:41,700
And lots of pages for Richard's photos of Max.

85
00:04:41,700 --> 00:04:44,700
Speaking of mother and of father

86
00:04:44,700 --> 00:04:47,647
--and speaking of Max--I hear the car.

87
00:04:47,647 --> 00:04:48,200
They're here!

88
00:04:48,200 --> 00:04:53,900
Oh! Oh, quickly! Go, go, go!

89
00:04:53,900 --> 00:04:56,776
Let's see. Oh, welcome home.

90
00:04:56,776 --> 00:04:57,400
Oh, let her in.

91
00:04:57,400 --> 00:04:58,900
Wait with your pictures for a second.

92
00:04:58,900 --> 00:05:01,300
Come on, darlings.

93
00:05:01,300 --> 00:05:05,900
Sweetheart .... Sit down right here.

94
00:05:05,900 --> 00:05:10,900
Oh, he's so cute! Oh, Marilyn!

95
00:05:10,900 --> 00:05:13,000
Max looks just like Grandpa.

96
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:14,600
A real Stewart.

97
00:05:14,600 --> 00:05:17,600
I'm so happy to be home with my family--and with Max.
